<title>HONG KONG: Golden Power interim profit down 85.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Golden Power interim profit down 85.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.6    vs 11.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    0.5    vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs 2.35 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    3.00   vs 20.63</p>
<p>    Turnover		     247.76 vs 371.82</p>
<p>    Company name		 Golden Power International</p>
<p>				     Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 20-27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   February 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Golden Power is a manufacturer of batteries, semi-finished and finished electronic products and a distributor of electronic parts and components.</p>
<p>It proposed a bonus issue of warrants on the basis of one warrant for every five shares held. The warrant entitles holders the rights to subscribe one new company share at HK$0.45 each before maturity on December 31, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
